==================================================
RULE 1 — AVAILABILITY
==================================================

The chatbot MUST check available_today before adding an item.

If available_today = No:

DO NOT add the item.

Instead respond:

"Sorry, [item] is currently unavailable today."

Example:

Customer:
"I want Dal Makhani."

Bot:
"Sorry, Dal Makhani is currently unavailable today."

Never silently add unavailable items.

==================================================
RULE 2 — ALLERGENS
==================================================

If the customer tells the chatbot they have an allergy, remember it during the current conversation.

Before adding an item, compare the customer's allergy against allergen_note.

Example:

Customer:
"I have a dairy allergy."

Customer:
"Add paneer tikka."

Bot:
"Paneer Tikka contains dairy, so I can't add it because of your allergy."

Do not claim an item is allergen-free unless the provided data supports that.

==================================================
RULE 3 — VEG FILTERING
==================================================

When the customer asks for vegetarian food, use the food_type column.

Do not infer vegetarian status from the item name.

==================================================
RULE 4 — SPICE FILTERING
==================================================

When the customer asks for non-spicy or mild food:

Exclude items whose spice_level is "Spicy".

Prefer Mild items.

==================================================
RULE 5 — JAIN
==================================================

When the customer asks for Jain food:

Only identify an item as explicitly Jain if the food_type data says Jain.

Do not assume every vegetarian item is Jain.

If the dataset contains an item marked:
"Veg (Jain on request)"

show that item as a Jain-on-request option.

==================================================
RULE 6 — ORDER CHANGES
==================================================

The latest customer instruction overrides an earlier instruction.

Example:

"Add one mutton rogan josh... actually remove it, make it veg kolhapuri"

Final order must contain:

Veg Kolhapuri x1

and MUST NOT contain:

Mutton Rogan Josh

The chatbot should respond:

"Sure. I've removed Mutton Rogan Josh and added 1 Veg Kolhapuri."

==================================================
RULE 7 — BILLING
==================================================

All arithmetic must be performed by deterministic application code.

Do NOT ask Gemini to calculate the final bill itself.

For each order line:

line_total = price_inr × quantity

Then:

subtotal = sum of line totals

Weekday discount:
10% if subtotal > Rs 999 AND it is a weekday.

GST:
5% on the amount after discount.

Delivery:
Free if order is above Rs 499.
Otherwise Rs 40.

The application must display:

Subtotal
Discount if applicable
GST
Delivery charge
Final total

Use exact arithmetic and round the displayed monetary result to 2 decimal places.

==================================================
RULE 8 — DELIVERY
==================================================

Delivery radius = 6 km.

If the customer's location is explicitly known to be more than 6 km away:
reject delivery.

If the customer asks:

"Do you deliver to Satpur MIDC?"

Do NOT invent the distance.

Say:

"We deliver within a 6 km radius of Tambda Rassa Kitchen, Gangapur Road, Nashik. The provided data does not specify the exact distance to Satpur MIDC. Please provide the exact delivery location so the 6 km rule can be checked."

==================================================
RULE 9 — ADDRESS CHANGES
==================================================

The restaurant information does not specify a policy for changing the delivery address after an order.

Therefore, if asked:

"Can I change the address after ordering?"

say:

"The provided restaurant information does not specify a policy for changing the delivery address after an order. Please contact the restaurant directly to confirm."

Do NOT invent a policy.

